title: "A U.S. county panel of skill specialization, relatedness, and complexity, across employer entity type"
abstract: >-
  A publicly available county-year panel of U.S. skill specialization,
  relatedness, and complexity, derived from 433.6 million Lightcast
  (formerly Burning Glass) job postings spanning 2010-2024. The panel
  covers 3,194 counties across 15 years (47,891 county-year observations)
  and reports 201 variables organized into eleven groups: a 37-variable
  core set describing the volume, employer-entity composition, work mode
  and internships, skill content, specialization, complexity, relatedness,
  and dynamics of local labor demand, plus 164 additional variables in the
  entity-decomposed extension covering entity-type specialization breadth,
  employer-pair skill-similarity, and per-employer-type dynamics for
  sectoral and spillover research.
